1 LEXICAL
    A lexical function returns an integer or a string, in an expression
    (see HELP SYMBOL EXPRESSIONS) or between apostrophes.  Its arguments are
    expressions, in parentheses and separated by commas; an optional one may
    be left out, keeping its comma, and a function with no arguments still
    takes "()".  Its name may be shortened while it names only one of VMS's
    lexical functions (F$LEN is F$LENGTH; F$L is ambiguous).  A keyword
    argument (an item, a field) is spelled in full, in either case.

    Strings and data types:

        F$CVSI(bit, size, string)        a bit field, signed
        F$CVUI(bit, size, string)        a bit field, unsigned
        F$EDIT(string, edits)            COLLAPSE, COMPRESS, LOWERCASE,
                                         TRIM, UNCOMMENT, UPCASE (a list)
        F$ELEMENT(n, delimiter, string)  the nth element, from 0
        F$EXTRACT(offset, length, string)  part of a string, from 0
        F$FAO(control, arg...)           $FAO's directives (!AS, !UL, ...)
        F$INTEGER(expression)            the value as an integer
        F$LENGTH(string)                 the string's length
        F$LOCATE(substring, string)      its offset, or the length if absent
        F$STRING(expression)             the value as a string
        F$TYPE(symbol)                   INTEGER, STRING, PROCESS_CONTEXT,
                                         or "" (undefined)

    The process and its command environment:

        F$DIRECTORY()                    the default directory
        F$ENVIRONMENT(item)              DEPTH, PROCEDURE, DEFAULT, PROMPT,
                                         ON_SEVERITY, ON_CONTROL_Y,
                                         VERIFY_PROCEDURE, VERIFY_IMAGE,
                                         INTERACTIVE, MAX_DEPTH, PROTECTION,
                                         ...
        F$GETJPI(pid, item)              $GETJPI's items ("" for this
                                         process): PID, PRCNAM, USERNAME,
                                         UIC, CURPRIV, STATE, MODE, ...;
                                         the address space's FREP0VA and
                                         FREP1VA (eight hex digits, as
                                         OWNER; FREP0VA "" with no P0
                                         pages), FREPTECNT, and VIRTPEAK
        F$GETSYI(item [,node])           $GETSYI's items: NODENAME, VERSION,
                                         BOOTTIME, SID, HW_NAME ("VAX
                                         (govax)"), ...; the paging
                                         parameters; PAGEFILE_PAGE and
                                         PAGEFILE_FREE (the page file's
                                         size and free pages); the global
                                         section limits GBLSECTIONS,
                                         GBLPAGES, GBLPAGFIL, and what's
                                         left, FREE_GBLSECTS, FREE_GBLPAGES,
                                         CONTIG_GBLPAGES
        F$IDENTIFIER(identifier, type)   NAME_TO_NUMBER: an identifier's
                                         value (0 if there's none);
                                         NUMBER_TO_NAME: its name ("")
        F$MODE()                         INTERACTIVE
        F$PID(context)                   each process's PID in turn, then
                                         "" (set context to "" first)
        F$CONTEXT("PROCESS", context, item [,value] [,qualifier])
                                         makes F$PID return only the
                                         processes whose item (PRCNAM,
                                         USERNAME, OWNER, GRP, PRI, UIC,
                                         CURPRIV, STATE, MODE, ...) matches
                                         a value: EQL or NEQ, for a number
                                         LSS, LEQ, GTR, GEQ, for CURPRIV
                                         ALL or ANY; item CANCEL ends it
        F$PRIVILEGE(privileges)          TRUE if they're enabled (and those
                                         named NOxxx aren't)
        F$PROCESS()                      the process's name
        F$SETPRV(privileges)             enables (NOxxx disables); returns
                                         what they were
        F$USER()                         the UIC, "[SYSTEM]"
        F$VERIFY([procedure] [,image])   returns verification (1 or 0),
                                         and sets it

    Files, devices, logical names, messages, and time:

        F$GETDVI(device, item)           $GETDVI's items: EXISTS, MNT,
                                         VOLNAM, FREEBLOCKS, DEVNAM, ...
        F$DEVICE([name] [,class] [,type] [,stream])
                                         the next device whose name matches
                                         (with * and %), of the class (DISK,
                                         TERM, MAILBOX, ...) and type, then
                                         ""
        F$FILE_ATTRIBUTES(file, item)    an attribute from the file's
                                         header: ORG, RFM, RAT, MRS, LRL,
                                         ALQ, EOF, FFB, CDT, RDT, PRO, UIC,
                                         FID, DID, DIRECTORY, VERLIMIT, ...
        F$PARSE(file [,default] [,related] [,field] [,type])
                                         the full file specification, or a
                                         field: NODE, DEVICE, DIRECTORY,
                                         NAME, TYPE, VERSION; type
                                         SYNTAX_ONLY or NO_CONCEAL
        F$SEARCH(file [,stream])         the next file that matches, then ""
        F$LOGICAL(name)                  a logical name's translation
        F$TRNLNM(name [,table] [,index] [,mode] [,case] [,item])
                                         a translation, or an item:
                                         VALUE, MAX_INDEX, TABLE_NAME,
                                         ACCESS_MODE, CONCEALED, LENGTH, ...
        F$MESSAGE(status)                a status's message text
        F$TIME()                         the date and time now
        F$CVTIME([time] [,format] [,field])
                                         a time in COMPARISON (yyyy-mm-dd
                                         hh:mm:ss.cc), ABSOLUTE, or DELTA
                                         format, or a field: DATE, TIME,
                                         YEAR, MONTH, DAY, WEEKDAY, ...

    F$CSID, F$GETQUI, and F$LICENSE are not here: govax has no cluster,
    queues, or licenses for them to report.

    govax has one lexical function VMS doesn't, for its configuration (see
    HELP CONFIG KEYS):

        F$CONFIG(key [,operation])       VALUE (the default): the item's
                                         value, or "" if it isn't set;
                                         EXISTS: 1 if it's set, else 0;
                                         BOOLEAN: 1 if its value is
                                         TRUE, T, YES, Y, or 1 (any
                                         case), else 0

    The key is a configuration item's name, such as "vax.startup.procedure",
    in either case.

    Examples:

        $ LEN = F$LENGTH(NAME) + 1
        $ GROUP = F$EXTRACT(1, F$LOCATE(",", UIC) - 1, UIC)
        $ IF F$SEARCH("TEMP.DAT") .NES. "" THEN DELETE TEMP.DAT;*
        $ IF F$TRNLNM("NAMES") .EQS. "" THEN DEFINE NAMES EMPLOYEES.DAT
        $ WRITE_TIME = F$CVTIME(,,"TIME")
        $ IF F$CONFIG("vax.library", "EXISTS") THEN -
              WRITE SYS$OUTPUT F$CONFIG("vax.library")
